      "content": "I hear how exhausting it is to feel like your efforts are falling on empty air when everything feels so hollow and unrewarding. Your analogy of trying to anchor a cloud makes perfect sense because that level of detachment often makes standard coping strategies feel incredibly frustrating, not because they don't work, but because the signal feels too weak to connect to anything. Even in its most unreal state, the effort to understand these feelings is a deeply human response that proves your presence and concern, even when the environment makes that presence feel impossible to verify.",
